1
00:03:51,724 --> 00:03:57,724
Someone has taken their love of scary movies one step too far.
Solving this mystery is going to be murder.

2
00:07:43,448 --> 00:07:49,448
Scream is a crime, horror, mystery film directed by Wes Craven.

3
00:11:35,172 --> 00:11:41,172
A year after the murder of her mother, a teenage girl is terrorized by a masked killer who
targets her and her friends by using scary movies as part of a deadly game.

4
00:15:26,896 --> 00:15:32,896
Dewey Riley, played by David Arquette.

5
00:19:18,620 --> 00:19:24,620
Sidney Prescott, played by Neve Campbell.

6
00:23:10,344 --> 00:23:16,344
Gale Weathers, played by Courteney Cox.

7
00:27:02,068 --> 00:27:08,068
Stu Macher, played by Matthew Lillard.

8
00:30:53,793 --> 00:30:59,793
Tatum Riley, played by Rose McGowan.

9
00:34:45,517 --> 00:34:51,517
Billy Loomis, played by Skeet Ulrich.

10
00:38:37,241 --> 00:38:43,241
Scream is a 1996 American slasher film directed by Wes
Craven and written by Kevin Williamson.

11
00:42:28,965 --> 00:42:34,965
It stars David Arquette, Neve Campbell, Courteney Cox, Matthew
Lillard, Rose McGowan, Skeet Ulrich, and Drew Barrymore.

12
00:46:20,689 --> 00:46:26,689
Set in the fictional town of Woodsboro, California, the plot follows high school student Sidney Prescott (Campbell) and her
friends, who, on the anniversary of her mother's murder, become the targets of a costumed serial killer.

13
00:50:12,413 --> 00:50:18,413
Williamson, who was struggling to get his projects off the ground, was inspired by reports of a series of murders by the Gainesville Ripper as he wrote a screenplay that
satirized the clichés of the slasher genre popularized in films such as Halloween (1978), Friday the 13th (1980), and Craven's own A Nightmare on Elm Street (1984).

14
00:54:04,137 --> 00:54:10,137
Developed under the title Scary Movie, Williamson's script became the subject of an intense bidding war from
multiple studios before Miramax Films purchased the rights for its Dimension Films label.

15
00:57:55,862 --> 00:58:01,862
Craven, despite turning down the opportunity multiple times, agreed to direct the film after he had read
the script as he was determined to re-establish himself after several career setbacks.

16
01:01:47,586 --> 01:01:53,586
The involvement of Barrymore and Cox helped secure more support from the studio.

17
01:05:39,310 --> 01:05:45,310
Principal photography took place from April to June 1996
in California on a budget of $15 million.

18
01:09:31,034 --> 01:09:37,034
Craven trimmed down the violence in the film after being involved in a tense conflict with
the Motion Picture Association of America (MPAA) over the desired R rating.

19
01:13:22,758 --> 01:13:28,758
Released on December 20, Scream was not expected to perform well due to concerns over
releasing a slasher film in a time normally reserved for holiday entertainment.

20
01:17:14,482 --> 01:17:20,482
However, it went on to gross approximately $173 million worldwide through the strength of word of
mouth, becoming an unexpected success and one of the highest-grossing films of the year.

21
01:21:06,206 --> 01:21:12,206
Contemporary reviews were positive, with praise going to the performances of its cast and its unique meta humor,
but criticism was directed at its excessive violence and lack of suspense in favor of that humor.

22
01:24:57,931 --> 01:25:03,931
Scream revitalized both Craven's and Barrymore's careers and
helped bolster the careers of its young cast.

23
01:28:49,655 --> 01:28:55,655
In the years since its release, Scream's reception has continued to be positive.

24
01:32:41,379 --> 01:32:47,379
It has been credited with rekindling interest in the horror genre during the 1990s following a decline in the genre's
popularity and has been credited for shifting the genre towards younger audiences and casting established actors.

25
01:36:33,103 --> 01:36:39,103
The film's opening sequence, in which Barrymore's character is killed by Ghostface, is
considered one of the most shocking and subversive in cinematic history.

26
01:40:24,827 --> 01:40:30,827
The success of the film launched a multimedia franchise, which comprises the sequels Scream 2 (1997), Scream 3 (2000), Scream
4 (2011), Scream (2022), Scream VI (2023), and Scream 7 (2026), as well as an anthology television series.

27
01:44:16,551 --> 01:44:22,551
The film explores themes of high school, small town, riddle, killing, halloween.

28
01:48:08,275 --> 01:48:14,275
The tone is dark and mind_bending.
